    title: "Day 5 — The Theology of the Cross",
    category: "novenas",
    day: 5,
    intention: "To love the Cross as the way to God",
    text: `O Saint Bonaventure, you taught that the Cross of Christ is the supreme mystery of the Christian faith and the door to all contemplation. You wrote: "Other doctors have explained the Scriptures, but you have explained the Cross of Christ." You saw in the Crucified One not defeat but the ultimate victory of love, not suffering alone but suffering transformed by divine charity. I pray today that I may embrace the Cross with the love and understanding that you brought to it. Help me to see beyond the scandal of the Cross to the glory it reveals, beyond the suffering it demands to the joy it promises. When I am called to suffer, let me look to the Crucified Christ, who suffered first and who suffers still in His members. O Bonaventure, doctor of the Cross, teach me to find God in the place of sacrifice. Amen.`,
