    category: "novenas",
    day: 6,
    intention: "To unite faith and reason in the pursuit of truth",
    text: `O Saint Bonaventure, you harmonized the pursuit of knowledge with the love of God. You studied at the University of Paris, you mastered the philosophy of Aristotle, and you engaged the intellectual currents of your time — all in the service of the Gospel. You taught that faith and reason are not enemies but allies, that the truths of philosophy and the truths of revelation come from the same divine Source. I pray today that my pursuit of knowledge may always be ordered toward the glory of God and the salvation of souls. Help me to study with diligence, to think with clarity, and to speak with charity. May my learning never make me proud, but always make me more grateful to God, more humble before the mystery, and more generous in the service of others. O Bonaventure, who united learning and holiness, obtain for me the grace to be both wise and holy. Amen.`,
