    category: "novenas",
    day: 7,
    intention: "To open my life to the gifts of the Holy Spirit",
    text: `O Saint Bonaventure, you taught with great insight the workings of the seven gifts of the Holy Spirit — wisdom, understanding, counsel, fortitude, knowledge, piety, and fear of the Lord. These gifts are not merely virtues that we acquire by effort but graces that the Holy Spirit implants in the soul, enabling us to respond to God's movements with docility and love. I pray today for a greater openness to the Holy Spirit in my life. Help me to recognize His movements, to cooperate with His inspirations, and to bear the fruit of His presence — love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, and self-control. Come, Holy Spirit, fill my heart with Your gifts, set my soul on fire with Your love, and guide me along the paths of righteousness. O Bonaventure, filled with the Holy Spirit, obtain for me the fullness of His sevenfold gifts. Amen.`,
