    category: "novenas",
    day: 8,
    intention: "To love Mary and to serve the Church",
    text: `O Saint Bonaventure, you had a profound devotion to the Blessed Virgin Mary, whom you honored as the Mother of God, the Mother of the Church, and the model of all holiness. You taught that Mary is the mirror of divine beauty, the garden enclosed, the star of the sea who guides the Church through the storms of this life. You also loved the Church with a pastoral heart, serving as Minister General of the Franciscan order and as Cardinal Bishop of Albano. I pray today that I may love Mary as you loved her, with tenderness, devotion, and confidence. Help me to honor her in my prayers, to imitate her in my virtues, and to trust her in my difficulties. And help me to love the Church — to pray for her, to serve her, to defend her, and to contribute to her mission of evangelization. O Bonaventure, devoted son of Mary and servant of the Church, obtain for me a heart like yours. Amen.`,
