    text: `O Saint Bonaventure, on this final day of my novena, I contemplate with you the supreme goal of the Christian life: the beatific vision — the direct, intuitive knowledge of God that is the happiness of heaven. You wrote that this vision is the ultimate fulfillment of every human desire, the end for which we were created, and the joy that surpasses all understanding. Help me to live this day and every day with this vision before my eyes. May the thought of heaven sustain me in trial, inspire me to holiness, and fill me with hope. I consecrate myself to the guidance of the Holy Spirit, to the protection of the Blessed Virgin Mary, and to the intercession of Saint Bonaventure. I ask you, O Seraphic Doctor, to pray for me now and at the hour of my death, that I may one day join you in the eternal vision of God, where love reigns forever and the song of heaven has no end. Amen.`,
